# Auth (register / login / logout)

This slice is **shipped**. Do not re-implement it. As-built details:
`ai-workspace/register-login-logout_prd.md`.

## What exists

- D1 `users` table via `migrations/0001_create_users.sql`
- `src/lib/password.ts` — `hashPassword` (trim + SHA-256 hex), `passwordHashesMatch`
- `src/lib/services/user-service.ts` — `createUser`, `getUserByUsername`,
  `getUserByEmail`, `updateUser`, `deleteUser`, `UserConflictError`
- `POST /api/register`, `POST /api/login`, `POST /api/logout`
- Pages: `/`, `/register` (`SignupForm`), `/login` (`LoginForm`), `/mcqs` stub

## Hard rules

- Hash the password **in the browser** with `hashPassword` from `@/lib/password`.
  POST `passwordHash` only. Never send plaintext. Never hash again on the server.
- Login is by **username**, not email. Username and email may be the same string
  for one user; uniqueness is still independent per column.
- Never import `user-service` (or any D1 module) into a `'use client'` file.
  Client forms `fetch` `/api/*`.
- Get D1 with `await getCloudflareContext({ async: true })`, then `env.DB`.
- Success JSON is a `PublicUser` (no `passwordHash`). Login 401 message is always
  `"Invalid username or password"`.
- There are **no sessions, cookies, or tokens**. Logout only POSTs `/api/logout`
  then navigates to `/login`. `/mcqs` is reachable by URL. Do not add JWT, OAuth,
  cookies, or middleware unless the user asks.
- Do not add bcrypt, an auth library, or `react-hook-form` unless asked.

## Forms

Auth UIs are client components (Web Crypto). Use shadcn `field` + `FieldError`,
not a Form component. No Google button. No forgot-password link.

## Next feature

MCQ work extends `/mcqs`. Reuse this auth. If writes must be teacher-only, ask
before adding sessions — do not silently protect the route.
